WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:03.068
WIL WILLIS: Braxton,
Jake, congratulations.

00:00:03.168 --> 00:00:04.070
You fellas have made
it to the third round

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:05.304
of this competition.

00:00:05.404 --> 00:00:06.940
Now we're sending
you back to your home

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.209
forges just to make this
iconic weapon from history--

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:15.681
the nagamaki.

00:00:15.781 --> 00:00:16.949
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:18.118
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:24.557
BRAXTON: It's day one.

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:26.659
I'm back at the home forge.

00:00:26.725 --> 00:00:32.298
I'm pretty nervous going to
make my first Japanese sword.

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:37.236
The first thing I do is
taking it down to size.

00:00:37.336 --> 00:00:40.506
Straightening this
blade is a hassle.

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:42.375
It's wanting to
curve like a banana,

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:46.378
and I'm having to straighten
it out little by little.

00:00:46.478 --> 00:00:50.517
I had to be very meticulous
on the amount of curve it has.

00:00:57.923 --> 00:00:58.991 line:7%
 It's the start of day two.

00:00:59.091 --> 00:01:00.526
And I'm ready to
get to work and try

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:03.062
and get this blade quenched--
fire 'em up, get 'em hot.

00:01:03.128 --> 00:01:04.363
I've never welded
anything that big,

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:05.865
and I really just
can't wait to test it.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:07.833
I can't wait to swing that
thing around in the yard just

00:01:07.933 --> 00:01:09.669
to have a feel for how it is.

00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:18.010
I check the blade,
and it's hard.

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:19.212
It's straight.

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:21.147
And I just have such
a sense of relief.

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.316
Let's hack at something,
see if it's going to break.

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:28.955
Just like that.

00:01:29.021 --> 00:01:31.524
It snapped the tip off about
six inches down from the tip.

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:33.760
I will not be able to meet
parameters with this blade,

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:36.662
so I decide to
start a new blade.

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:37.931
Son of a bitch.

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:39.165
You know, I probably
had a stress fracture.

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:40.733
The grain in there
is pretty tight.

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:46.372
I got half a day left to hammer
out and forge out a blade.

00:01:49.541 --> 00:01:51.544 line:0%
BRAXTON: Now that I've
got the blade done,

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:52.411 line:7%
we got the hibachi done.

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:56.315 line:0%
And now it's time
to do the tsuba.

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:57.883
The guard is very important.

00:01:57.983 --> 00:01:59.652
Everything needs to be smooth.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:01.488
Ugh, that's a tight fit.

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:02.689
Feels really good.

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:04.356
It's just a little bit heavy.

00:02:04.423 --> 00:02:08.027
The nagamaki being too heavy
can make it unwieldable

00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:11.163
and make it uncomfortable
to swing around.

00:02:11.263 --> 00:02:12.265
That's right where the guard is.

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:13.900
It's a little heavy.

00:02:13.966 --> 00:02:17.903
I mill a simple pattern into
the tsuba to lose some weight.

00:02:18.003 --> 00:02:21.774
Actually feels a lot better now.

00:02:21.874 --> 00:02:25.310
All I lack is the wrapping
and doing a final cleanup.

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:29.681
I only have a few little
things to do on day four.

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:30.650
This is cool.

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:35.021 line:0%
JACK: My last day I
had so much to do.

00:02:35.121 --> 00:02:37.323 line:7%
I have no room for error.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:39.825
I was able to forge
out a blade, grind

00:02:39.892 --> 00:02:41.160
it out, and get it quenched.

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:43.696
So I'm just going to try
and meet the parameters

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:46.232
and get the blade
turned in and sharp.

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:48.000
That's pretty good.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.368
I have my hibachi done.

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:51.004
That took me a long
time yesterday.

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:54.039
I have my tsuba pretty
much to where I want it.

00:02:54.106 --> 00:02:55.842
My main goal for
today in general

00:02:55.909 --> 00:02:57.476
is just to get the
handle complete.

00:02:57.576 --> 00:02:59.312
I'm quickly running out of time.

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:02.948
I need to make this handle
as quickly and as efficiently

00:03:03.048 --> 00:03:04.583
as possible.

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:06.920
I'm trying to get a pretty good
grip on to where the blade is

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.220
very easily indexed.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:10.256
I don't want the
handle to be too thick.

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:13.826
But honestly, I just need
to get a handle on it.

00:03:13.926 --> 00:03:16.495
It's solid That's for sure.

00:03:16.595 --> 00:03:18.664
Once the glue dries
on the leather wrap,

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:22.835
I go ahead and start this
long process of the ito wrap.

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:24.903
This just so happens to
be one of the hardest

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:26.372
builds I've ever done.

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:27.540
I really could have
used an extra day,

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:31.277
but I'm just happy
that it's over.

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:33.245
Oh, that is smooth!

00:03:33.312 --> 00:03:34.413
DOUG MARCAIDA: All
right, bladesmiths.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.581
I will take your
weapons to deliver

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:37.817
killing blows,
slashes, and thrusts

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:40.219
on this wild boar carcass.

00:03:40.319 --> 00:03:41.320
Braxton, you're up first.

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:42.120
Are you ready for this?

00:03:42.187 --> 00:03:42.888
 I'm ready.

00:03:42.955 --> 00:03:43.756
[inaudible]

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:44.857
 Let's do this.

00:03:44.923 --> 00:03:46.092
BRAXTON: Oh, man.

00:03:46.158 --> 00:03:47.526
We have a hogs around
where I'm from.

00:03:47.626 --> 00:03:49.328
The skin is very, very thick.

00:03:49.394 --> 00:03:52.264
I'm nervous, but there
is nothing I can do.

00:03:52.331 --> 00:03:56.869
I just gotta let the
chips fall where they lay.

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:59.839
[rock music]

00:04:13.953 --> 00:04:15.354
 All right, Braxton.

00:04:15.454 --> 00:04:20.159
Your nagamaki here is
definitely not boring.

00:04:20.225 --> 00:04:22.061
It is razor sharp.

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:25.231
Every cut with this
thick wild boar carcass

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:28.200
allowed me to peel off
layers of the very thick hide

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:29.502
that it has.

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:33.172
Also, the lightness that
you have with this blade

00:04:33.239 --> 00:04:35.041
allows for switching
with the grip here.

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:36.842
It's got very good
grip in the handle.

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:40.279
I can index exactly were
the edge is at all times.

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:44.683
Overall, sir, your
nagamaki will kill.

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:46.151
 Thank you.

00:04:46.251 --> 00:04:47.085
 All right, Jake.

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:48.086
It's your turn.

00:04:48.187 --> 00:04:48.820
Ready for this?

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:49.956
 Chop him up.

00:04:50.023 --> 00:04:51.590
 Let's do this.

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:53.293
JAKE: It makes me a
little bit nervous.

00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:55.227
I really want mine to chop
through the boar as well.

00:04:55.327 --> 00:04:57.563
But the blade can actually
take a lot of damage

00:04:57.630 --> 00:05:01.600
during the boar testing
because there's bones.

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:04.403
I know that Braxton's
blade set a very high bar.

00:05:04.469 --> 00:05:07.205
Mine needs to perform
just as good as his.

00:05:07.272 --> 00:05:09.709
[rock music]

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:28.027
DOUG MARCAIDA: All right, Jake.

00:05:28.094 --> 00:05:29.695
Let's talk about
your nagamaki here.

00:05:29.795 --> 00:05:30.796
It's sharp.

00:05:30.896 --> 00:05:33.866
Wielding this weapon
is a lot of fun also.

00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:36.602
The weight you have here
and the balance works.

00:05:36.702 --> 00:05:39.972
Overall, sir, your
nagamaki will kill.

00:05:40.072 --> 00:05:41.040
 Thank you.

00:05:41.106 --> 00:05:43.041
 Next up is the strength test.

00:05:43.108 --> 00:05:43.743
Dave?

00:05:46.579 --> 00:05:48.514
 Now, to test the strength
and overall construction

00:05:48.581 --> 00:05:50.850
of your blades, I'll be
chopping into this bamboo.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:54.286
Now, this test is not about what
your blades do to the bamboo--

00:05:54.353 --> 00:05:56.489
what the bamboo
does to your blades.

00:05:56.589 --> 00:05:57.323
Braxton, you're up first.

00:05:57.423 --> 00:05:58.123
You ready?

00:05:58.190 --> 00:05:58.858
 I'm ready.

00:06:07.232 --> 00:06:10.370
[rock music]

00:06:26.219 --> 00:06:27.753
 All right, Braxton.

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:30.490
As far as what the bamboo did
to your blade, it did nothing.

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:34.460
There's no deflection, rolls,
chips, anything on this blade.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:36.161
It's as sharp as
when I picked it up.

00:06:36.228 --> 00:06:37.129
Nicely done.

00:06:37.229 --> 00:06:37.964
It's a very strong blade.

00:06:38.064 --> 00:06:39.165
 Thank you so much.

00:06:39.231 --> 00:06:39.965
 All right, Jake.

00:06:40.032 --> 00:06:40.932
You're ready?

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:41.667
 Let's do it.

00:06:50.743 --> 00:06:53.613
[rock music]

00:07:05.157 --> 00:07:06.492
 All right.

00:07:06.559 --> 00:07:08.594
So your edge, just as
sharp as when it started.

00:07:08.661 --> 00:07:10.796
There are no chips,
rolls, defamation.

00:07:10.863 --> 00:07:14.300
It sliced right
through the bamboo.

00:07:14.367 --> 00:07:18.304
Your handle is a little
wide this way for me.

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:19.871
But the fact that
it's lean this way

00:07:19.972 --> 00:07:23.375
and that that wrap's so
nice and comfortable is--

00:07:23.476 --> 00:07:24.343
evens it out.

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:25.111
Well done.

00:07:25.178 --> 00:07:25.845
JAKE: Thank you.

00:07:28.047 --> 00:07:29.015
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:30.282
We know your blades can kill.

00:07:30.349 --> 00:07:31.684
We know they're strong.

00:07:31.751 --> 00:07:33.785
Now it's time to find
out how sharp they are.

00:07:33.852 --> 00:07:35.321
Now, unlike the
strength test, this

00:07:35.387 --> 00:07:37.756
is all about what
your edge will do

00:07:37.823 --> 00:07:40.359
to these different
materials, from the tatami,

00:07:40.459 --> 00:07:42.828
the melons, or the sandbags.

00:07:42.928 --> 00:07:44.396
Braxton, you're up first.
You ready for this?

00:07:44.463 --> 00:07:45.131
 I'm ready.

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:57.477
[rock music]

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:12.558
DOUG MARCAIDA: All
right, Braxton.

00:08:12.658 --> 00:08:14.293
Your edge had no
issues at all cutting

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:15.694
through the tatami mats.

00:08:15.761 --> 00:08:17.062
Cuts the melon easily.

00:08:17.129 --> 00:08:19.632
And on the sandbags,
it will cut through.

00:08:19.699 --> 00:08:23.001
Overall, sir, your
weapon, it will cut.

00:08:23.068 --> 00:08:24.136
 Thank you.

00:08:24.203 --> 00:08:25.437
DOUG MARCAIDA: Jake, your turn.
Are you ready?

00:08:25.538 --> 00:08:26.172
 Let's do it.

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:34.580
[rock music]

00:08:52.297 --> 00:08:53.465
DOUG MARCAIDA: All right, Jake.

00:08:53.565 --> 00:08:55.167
Let's talk about you
nagamaki right here--

00:08:55.234 --> 00:08:56.235
razor sharp.

00:08:56.301 --> 00:08:58.204
It cuts easily on the tatami.

00:08:58.271 --> 00:08:59.738
Cuts the melons.

00:08:59.805 --> 00:09:02.574
And just off the orders of
the corners, it cut it easily.

00:09:02.641 --> 00:09:05.210
Overall, sir, it will cut.

00:09:05.277 --> 00:09:06.445
 Thank you.

00:09:06.512 --> 00:09:07.547
 This is going to
be very hard for us.

00:09:10.582 --> 00:09:11.683
WIL WILLIS:
Bladesmiths, the judges

00:09:11.783 --> 00:09:14.053
have made their final decision.

00:09:14.119 --> 00:09:19.258
The new "Forged in Fire"
champion is Braxton.

00:09:19.325 --> 00:09:21.894
Congratulations, you're the
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:21.961 --> 00:09:24.729
Jake, unfortunately your
blade didn't make the cut.

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:26.298
Ben Abbott's going
to tell you why.

00:09:26.365 --> 00:09:27.666
 Well, Jake, you
should be proud.

00:09:27.732 --> 00:09:29.935
You made a beautiful
and effective weapon.

00:09:30.035 --> 00:09:32.505
And for us this came down
to the finest of points--

00:09:32.572 --> 00:09:34.540
the fact that your blade
wasn't quite as finished,

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:36.708
and we had a slight preference
for Braxton's handle.

00:09:36.775 --> 00:09:38.577
And that's the reason
we're sending you home.

00:09:38.643 --> 00:09:41.613
 Jake, please,
surrender your blade.

00:09:41.713 --> 00:09:43.215
JAKE: I think the
time frame that I

00:09:43.281 --> 00:09:46.352
had to build my second blade
definitely had a factor in it.

00:09:46.452 --> 00:09:47.919
I may not be the "Forged
in Fire" champion,

00:09:48.019 --> 00:09:49.455
but I feel like I
accomplished a lot

00:09:49.521 --> 00:09:53.358
and earned the
privilege to be here.

00:09:53.425 --> 00:09:54.727
 Braxton, congratulations.

00:09:54.793 --> 00:09:56.261
You're the "Forged
in Fire" champion,

00:09:56.361 --> 00:09:58.230
and that's a title that comes
with a check for 10 grand.

00:09:58.297 --> 00:09:58.964
Good job.

00:09:59.031 --> 00:10:00.198
[applause]

00:10:00.265 --> 00:10:03.069
BRAXTON: I feel great about
what I've accomplished.

00:10:03.135 --> 00:10:04.203
I'm still shaking.

00:10:04.303 --> 00:10:06.638
It was an awesome experience,
and I proved that I

00:10:06.738 --> 00:10:08.006
can hang with the big guys.

00:10:08.073 --> 00:10:10.343
[rock music]

